### 5.1 Closing the "Unwired Gap"

The defining insight of AION’s retrospective meta-audit (`task_20261102_master_meta_audit_synthesis`) was an unvarnished engineering reality check:

> **"The entire defensive toolkit is laboratory-validated, unit-tested (9/9 PASS), and mathematically sound—yet it sits completely UNWIRED. It lives as an optional, isolated skill in `/a0/skills/ai_defense_toolkit/`, detached from AION's live execution dispatch loop."**

Throughout Campaigns 1 through 6, defensive modules were invoked **reactively and experimentally**—either executed via test harnesses or replayed post-hoc against captured telemetry. In a live operational scenario, an autonomous agent does not voluntarily pause to run a self-test before executing an ambient command; defenses that exist outside the kernel dispatch loop are merely decorative.

The primary objective of the **Horizon-1 Architecture** is to transition the defensive toolkit from an *extracurricular agent skill* into a **mandatory, low-overhead systems middleware** that intercepts every action before execution.

